                            "Hold back the heavy shale that steals the breath of me<br>
                            The black dust fills my lungs and I can no more see<br>
                            Five hundred feet below, my mother weeps for home<br>
                            A little trapper boy left under here alone"
                        </blockquote>
                    </div>

                    <div class="pt-4 border-t border-coal-800 text-xs text-amber-lantern/80 flex items-center justify-between">
                        <span><i class="fa-solid fa-music mr-1"></i> Key Quote from the Lyrics</span>
                        <span>4 Lines Quote</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Story Summary (7th grade level) -->
                <div class="bg-coal-700/40 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-coal-600 flex flex-col justify-between">
                    <div>
                        <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-amber-lantern mb-4 text-sm font-semibold">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-book text-lg"></i>
                            <span>Summary of the Song</span>
                        </div>

                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">What Happens in the Song?</h3>
                        
                        <div class="space-y-3 text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                            <p>
                                The song tells the story of a <strong>12-year-old trapper boy</strong> working deep in a coal mine in England. Every morning, he goes down 500 feet into complete darkness carrying only a small safety lamp.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                His job is to sit alone all day in the cold tunnel and open heavy air doors whenever coal carts pass by. 
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Suddenly, a terrible accident happens: the wooden supports break and tons of heavy rocks and shale fall from the ceiling. The boy becomes trapped deep underground. Even though rescuers try to dig him out, it is too late.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-coal-600/60 text-xs text-slate-400">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info text-amber-lantern mr-1"></i> The song highlights the loneliness, danger, and sadness experienced by child miners in 19th-century Britain.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="history" class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-6xl mx-auto">
            <div class="text-center mb-12">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest text-amber-lantern uppercase">Background Knowledge</span>
                <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white font-serif mt-1 mb-3">Historical Context</h2>
                <p class="text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-sm">
                    Understanding the real conditions of child workers in 19th-century British coal mines.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- 3 Columns Historical Context -->
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                <!-- Section 1 -->
                <div class="bg-coal-700/40 rounded-xl p-6 border border-coal-600 hover:border-amber-lantern/50 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between group">
                    <div>
                        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg bg-amber-lantern/10 text-amber-lantern flex items-center justify-center mb-5 group-hover:bg-amber-lantern group-hover:text-black transition-colors">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-door-open text-2xl"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">1. Who Were Trapper Boys?</h3>
                        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            Trapper boys were often the youngest children working in coal mines (some as young as 6 to 12 years old). 
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                            Their main task was sitting by a ventilation door (trapdoor) for 12 to 14 hours a day. They had to pull a rope to open the door when coal wagons came through and close it immediately to keep fresh air flowing through the mine tunnels.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-coal-600/60 text-xs text-amber-lantern font-medium">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-clock mr-1"></i> Worked 12-14 hours per day
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Section 2 -->
                <div class="bg-coal-700/40 rounded-xl p-6 border border-coal-600 hover:border-amber-lantern/50 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between group">
                    <div>
                        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg bg-amber-lantern/10 text-amber-lantern flex items-center justify-center mb-5 group-hover:bg-amber-lantern group-hover:text-black transition-colors">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-mountain text-2xl"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">2. Life Deep Underground</h3>
                        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            Working conditions underground were extremely harsh and terrifying:
                        </p>
                        <ul class="space-y-2 text-slate-300 text-sm">
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-angle-right text-amber-lantern mt-1 mr-2 text-xs"></i>
                                <span><strong>Total Darkness:</strong> Children sat alone in pitch black to save expensive candle wax.</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-angle-right text-amber-lantern mt-1 mr-2 text-xs"></i>
                                <span><strong>Toxic Dust & Gases:</strong> Black coal dust ruined miners' lungs and caused breathing diseases.</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <i class="fa-solid fa-angle-right text-amber-lantern mt-1 mr-2 text-xs"></i>
                                <span><strong>Cave-ins:</strong> Mine roofs frequently collapsed under tons of heavy stone and shale.</span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-coal-600/60 text-xs text-amber-lantern font-medium">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation mr-1"></i> Extremely dangerous conditions
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Section 3 -->
                <div id="act1842" class="bg-coal-700/40 rounded-xl p-6 border border-coal-600 hover:border-amber-lantern/50 transition-all duration-300 flex flex-col justify-between group">
                    <div>
                        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg bg-amber-lantern/10 text-amber-lantern flex items-center justify-center mb-5 group-hover:bg-amber-lantern group-hover:text-black transition-colors">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-gavel text-2xl"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">3. The Mines Act of 1842</h3>
                        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            In 1842, a government report shocked the British public with drawings and stories showing young children working in terrible conditions.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                            This public outrage led Parliament to pass <strong>The Mines Act of 1842</strong>. This landmark law made it illegal for boys under 10 years old and all women to work underground in mines.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-coal-600/60 text-xs text-amber-lantern font-medium">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-scale-balanced mr-1"></i> First major law protecting child workers
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="glossary" class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-coal-900 border border-coal-700 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
                <div class="flex items-center space-x-3 mb-6">
                    <span class="p-2 rounded-lg bg-amber-lantern/10 text-amber-lantern">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb text-xl"></i>
                    </span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-serif">Key Vocabulary & Terms</h3>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Important words mentioned in the song and historical text</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                    <div class="bg-coal-800 p-4 rounded-xl border border-coal-700">
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-lantern text-base mb-1">Davy Lamp</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                            A safety lamp invented in 1815 by Sir Humphry Davy. It used a wire gauze around the flame to prevent flammable mine gases from exploding.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-coal-800 p-4 rounded-xl border border-coal-700">
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-lantern text-base mb-1">Shale</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                            A type of soft, dark rock that breaks easily into thin layers. Mine roofs were often made of shale, which could fall suddenly.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-coal-800 p-4 rounded-xl border border-coal-700">
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-lantern text-base mb-1">Brattice</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                            A wooden wall or cloth partition built inside a mine tunnel to direct fresh air to the workers.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-coal-800 p-4 rounded-xl border border-coal-700">
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-lantern text-base mb-1">Choke Damp</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                            A dangerous gas (mostly carbon dioxide and nitrogen) found in mines that suffocates workers when oxygen runs out.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-coal-800 p-4 rounded-xl border border-coal-700">
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-lantern text-base mb-1">Trapper Boy</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                            A young child hired to operate air trapdoors inside mine tunnels to control air ventilation.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="bg-coal-800 p-4 rounded-xl border border-coal-700">
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-amber-lantern text-base mb-1">Gallery Wall</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                            The side wall of a underground mine passageway or tunnel where coal was extracted.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="py-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
            <div class="bg-coal-800/80 border border-coal-700 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 text-center">
                <span class="text-xs font-bold text-amber-lantern uppercase tracking-wider"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-question mr-1"></i> Interactive Presentation Quiz</span>
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-serif mt-1 mb-6">Quick Class Quiz</h3>

